      "message": "The aforementioned bug was caused because we called `ShouldMethodBeCompiled()` before the locations were built in `AllocateRegisters()` during liveness analysis. In this patch it didn\u0027t cause an issue because we unconditionally rejected all instructions however in the [stage 2.1 setup](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2901291/5/compiler/optimizing/optimizing_compiler.cc#778) this allows instructions that haven\u0027t had their locations set yet, thus allowing all instructions and methods to pass through the filter.\n\nMoving `ShouldMethodBeCompiled()` after register allocation ensures that methods are correctly checked and rejected based on their instructions.",
